  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "PERCENTOF requires _xlfn., maps held array or reference errors to #NUM!, and coerces only direct scalars",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527.20088, PERCENTOF(data_subset, data_all) requires the _xlfn. prefix in OOXML (@PERCENTOF without _xlfn. gives #NAME?), divides SUM(data_subset) by SUM(data_all), coerces direct text and logicals (PERCENTOF(\"1\",4) = 0.25, PERCENTOF(TRUE,4) = 0.25) and omitted arguments (PERCENTOF(,4) = 0), skips text/logicals inside references or arrays, sums union areas, returns direct errors directly (#N/A -> #N/A), and maps any error held inside a reference or array to #NUM! (PERCENTOF(Data!A1:A3,Data!A1:E3) = #NUM! because Data!C1 holds #N/A). Matches 5,578/5,578 full-bank rows.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across all 16 rows of dch9u_functions and row 422 of prefix_metadata in Excel 16.0.20527.20088, plus 5,578/5,578 full-bank PERCENTOF witness rows.",
